## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant degradation control in real-time multi-hop pipelines under load.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health propagation across hops
- Per-tenant circuit-breakers and edge state
- Minute-by-minute control loops with queue depth and SLA awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example control logic sketch (pseudo)
type TenantState = { id:string; ckne:string; queue:number; sla:'high'|'medium'|'low'; mode:'OPEN'|'HALF'|'CLOSED' };
function tick(states:TenantState[]) {
  for (const s of states){
    const th = s.sla==='high'? 100: s.sla==='medium'? 60: 40;
    if (s.ckne === 'red' || s.queue > th) s.mode = 'OPEN';
    else if (s.ckne === 'yellow') s.mode = 'HALF';
    else s.mode = 'CLOSED';
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a new CKNE angle at the edge: cross-tenant cache resource partitioning with live reallocation under traffic bursts.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE→cache-size mapping
- Eviction aggressiveness tuning
- Per-tenant prefetch priority
- Minute-by-minute shard reallocation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-policy skeleton
function policyForTenant(ckne) {
  // map to allocation, eviction, prefetch
  const size = baseSize * (0.5 + ckne);
  const evict = Math.max(1, Math.floor(5 * (1 - ckne)));
  const prefetch = Math.round(10 * ckne);
  return {size, evict, prefetch};
}
```

